    "result_text": "The full suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS` (AcceptanceBase and AuditLogCapture are support classes, not test classes). The implementation is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule for `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is now rejected with **409** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in this repo, I added a new pipeline step modeled on the existing `RejectDuplicate*` functions:\n\n- **`RejectCityAtCapacity`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 reads the `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` request, counts existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed, consistent with `RejectDuplicateHousehold`), and throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the count is \u2265 50.\n- **`CityAtCapacityException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) so it surfaces as an escalation.\n- **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with an `{\"errors\": ...}` body, matching `DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler`.\n- **Escalation YAML** `officefloor/escalation/...CityAtCapacityException.yml` mapping the exception to the handler.\n- Wired the new `rejectCityAtCapacity` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `rejectDuplicateHousehold` and `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fill a fresh city to 50, expect the 51st to 409) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
